[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Tool execution, equivalence, latency scheduling, performance and documentation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TOOL-RUN-001
TITLE: Literal subprocess arguments and retained evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
The HDL runner shall execute absolute programs without a shell, preserve separate
arguments, drain stdout/stderr concurrently with finite per-stream byte limits,
close stdin and retain raw logs and JSON provenance in a new artifact directory.
Nonzero exit, absent/unstartable executable and truncated output shall not succeed.
Implementation: SharpHDL.Tooling.HdlToolRunner and SharpHDL.ToolCli.
Verification: HdlToolRunnerTests, generated argv properties and run-scheduled-rtl.sh.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TOOL-RUN-002
TITLE: Cancellable ordinary process trees
STATEMENT: >>>
The runner shall distinguish caller cancellation from deadline expiry, terminate
the ordinary process tree and observe pipe tasks before returning. Cleanup/IO
errors shall propagate. Detached/reparented daemon containment is unsupported;
the runner is not a sandbox. Evidence directories shall never be overwritten.
Verification: Cancellation_terminates_an_ordinary_process_tree and timeout/limit tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BV-EQUIV-001
TITLE: Bounded combinational equivalence with no silent omissions
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall compare two outputs over all matching ordinal input valuations
using real Z3 4.12.2 bit vectors. Support only 1..256-node combinational graphs,
1..32-bit values and at most 128 total input bits with unique bounded ASCII input
identifiers. Reject every state boundary, RAM, ROM and DSP primitive, including
unused unsupported nodes. Explicit signed operations, modular arithmetic, shifts,
slices, zero/sign extension and concatenation shall preserve Core semantics.
Implementation: SharpHDL.Verification.BitVectorEquivalence.
Verification: complete small truth tables, CLR arithmetic properties and independent
Yosys checks in SharpHDL.EquivalenceCli. This is not sequential equivalence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BV-EQUIV-002
TITLE: Retained counterexamples and nonproof outcomes
STATEMENT: >>>
Only a completed UNSAT result shall denote Equivalent. SAT valuations shall
reproduce differing outputs in the independent Core evaluator before Different
is returned. Retain SMT-LIB, native version and concrete decimal input values.
Resource exhaustion/timeout, cancellation, unsupported inputs and unavailable or
mismatched native assets shall never be classified as equivalent. Retain actual
Yosys counterexamples in the independent qualification campaign.
Counterexample evaluation shall bound constant shifts by the hardware result
width before host arithmetic, avoiding unbounded intermediate BigInteger allocation.
Verification: Native_resource_exhaustion_and_precancellation_do_not_prove_equivalence,
profile rejection tests, deliberately corrupted truth tables and retained native runs.
<<<
